1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,128
Imagine a normal morning, a few weeks from now, with SPECS on. You grab your keys, and MEMAR notices: collect the parcel before you leave.

2
00:00:10,428 --> 00:00:15,852
At the door, it checks the things you carry. Take the umbrella; it rains after five.

3
00:00:17,052 --> 00:00:21,300
In the kitchen, your daily vitamin D is waiting right on the box.

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,504
And the fridge remembers the milk for the way back.

5
00:00:25,704 --> 00:00:30,000
At your desk, one look at the laptop: the report is due today.

6
00:00:30,299 --> 00:00:34,211
Pinch it done. No app to open, no phone to unlock.

7
00:00:35,562 --> 00:00:40,554
This is MEMAR. Memory, plus AR: reminders that live on your things.

8
00:00:41,854 --> 00:00:46,870
Reminder apps remember everything. They just don't remind you at the moment it matters.

9
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:54,104
So MEMAR puts each memory on the thing it belongs to, like a quiet assistant for your whole day.

10
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:57,694
Daily routines, like vitamin D after lunch.

11
00:00:58,044 --> 00:01:01,212
Things you always forget, like the charger in your bag.

12
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:03,770
Deadlines, right on your laptop.

13
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,992
Errands, on the fridge.

14
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:08,766
A quick check at the door before you leave.

15
00:01:09,116 --> 00:01:12,884
And you add them hands-free: look, pinch, or just say it.

16
00:01:14,034 --> 00:01:21,162
Here's the real Lens, in the SPECS preview of Lens Studio. Every object shows a badge with how many things are waiting.

17
00:01:22,462 --> 00:01:29,374
Look at something for a second and MEMAR locks on. Here it's simulated from head direction, and a pinch always confirms.

18
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:37,514
Pinch to open its memories, most urgent first. Done drops the badge, and Undo stays for eight seconds.

19
00:01:38,814 --> 00:01:46,110
Add from quick presets, or just say it. One sentence becomes a clean title, saved only when you pinch Save.

20
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:52,114
Turn to the entryway, and the door lists what's still pending on the things you carry.

21
00:01:53,414 --> 00:01:57,158
Tick off a daily routine, and it's back tomorrow by itself.

22
00:01:58,308 --> 00:02:03,876
Now watch it run live, on a phone, with the same memory engine. Done, and undo.

23
00:02:04,806 --> 00:02:06,966
Add to the notebook from a preset.

24
00:02:09,905 --> 00:02:15,617
Or say it in one sentence. It becomes a clean title, saved only when I tap Save.

25
00:02:17,278 --> 00:02:22,318
Vitamin D is a daily routine. Done, and it's already back for tomorrow.

26
00:02:22,931 --> 00:02:27,179
The door check updates, and the done list keeps everything I finished.

27
00:02:29,309 --> 00:02:38,333
MEMAR was built with CLAD and the Lens Studio MCP. All fourteen LEAF scenarios pass in the preview, and all forty one engine tests pass.

28
00:02:39,633 --> 00:02:46,713
Today the objects are stand-ins, because the preview can't see. Next comes real recognition, tested on SPECS.

29
00:02:48,013 --> 00:02:51,589
MEMAR. Your real world. Your memories.

